# The operator's own planning notes. UNANCHORED deliberately, and it has two effects
# rather than one: it hides a top-level `plans/`, and it is also what keeps the
# interactive CLI's own `.claude/plans/` out of the tree. Anchoring this pattern would
# silently start tracking the second.
plans/

# The operator's personal permission and hook overrides for their own interactive session.
# `.claude/settings.json` beside it IS committed: a permission or hook the workflow depends
# on belongs in a file every checkout carries. This one is per-operator scratch, and a
# checkout that tracked it would make one machine's ad-hoc grants everyone's.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Runtime state the interactive CLI writes beside its settings: scratch checkouts, the
# scheduler's state, per-session bookkeeping. Machine-local by construction, and none of it
# is a decision this repository makes. Listed here rather than in `.git/info/exclude`, which
# is where this checkout was carrying the whole set: that file is per-clone, so every fresh
# clone offers them for commit. The set is the CLI's, so it grows — an entry appearing here
# means one more thing the CLI writes, not one more decision.
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/checkpoints/
.claude/mailbox/
.claude/routines/.state/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/agent-registry.json
.claude/agent-memory-local
.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json
.claude/first-run

# The operator's own leaf-LLM configuration: the file run_workflow.py loads when nobody
# passes --llm-config. Which model runs which leaf is a local decision, so tracking it would
# force every operator who makes one to carry a permanent diff. Copy a sample from
# docs/examples/ to create it. ANCHORED, unlike the rest of this file: the contract is
# repo-root-relative, and an unanchored pattern would silently ignore a committed llm.yaml
# anywhere in the tree.
/llm.yaml

# Workspace artifacts generated by plan/generate/build/execute pipeline
workspace/
workspace_*/
workspace_backup_*/

# The operator's own Claude Code session transcripts, copied from the machine that ran the
# orchestrations this checkout carries. `skills/workflow-timing-audit/` reads them: a leaf's
# token record is not written into `workspace*/` at all (no orchestration_meta.json carries a
# `claude_workflow_home`), so the transcript under the operator's own `~/.claude/projects/`
# is the only source, and it is machine-local and expires on the CLI's cleanup schedule.
# Personal working aid, not a canonical record (`AGENTS.md` §Canonical record placement).
# ANCHORED, like /llm.yaml: this names one directory the operator created at the repository
# root, and an unanchored pattern would silently ignore a committed transcript_data/ anywhere.
/transcript_data/
.serena/
package-lock.json

# Python cache and test artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc.*
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Local virtual environments and dotenv files
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env
.env.*
.python-version
fortitude

# Editor and OS noise
.cursor/mcp.json
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Generic temporary/log files
*.log
*.tmp
command_log.jsonl

# rikyu-review-logs
.rikyu-review-logs/
review-tasks.json
review-experiment.json
